 R←Test_57(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;H;crash;name
⍝ `CreateFilename` names the files the way `CheckErrorFolder` names the default folder: "ERROR_WS" in a
⍝ clear workspace, and never an empty name. See also Test_24.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 H←##.HandleError
 crash←⎕NS''
 crash.WSID←'CLEAR WS'
 name←2⊃⎕NPARTS H.CreateFilename'C:/Temp/Errors'crash
 →T.GoToTidyUp' '∊name
 →T.GoToTidyUp'ERROR_WS_'≢9↑name

 crash.WSID←''                                       ⍝ A stand-alone EXE
 name←2⊃⎕NPARTS H.CreateFilename'C:/Temp/Errors'crash
 →T.GoToTidyUp'_'=⊃name

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
